+## Rolling Monitor & VRAM
+
+Start the rolling monitor with no warmup, wait for several rendered frames, then read and stop it without saving. Report the VRAM current/P95/peak usage, local-memory budget, peak timestamp, and over-budget frame rate. (Expected: `vram.available=true` on D3D12/Vulkan with `used`, `usage`, `current_used_mb`, `current_budget_mb`, `peak_time_seconds`, and `over_budget_pct`; explain that budget is the OS/driver process budget, not physical card capacity.)
+
+---
+
 ## Hitch Validation — CPU paths (self-measured, single response)
 
 Force a 250 ms hitch on the game thread and validate the verdict from that same response. Do NOT follow up with a frame_timing call — the CPU stall blocks the game thread, so a follow-up read reliably lands on a clean frame and misses it. (Expected: observed_peak_game_ms ≈ 250 or more and verdict_matched_expect=true, in the force_hitch response itself.)
